; A quarry causeway (issue #54, #53's FallingRock). Two banks flank a canyon;
; the only way across is a flat bridge straight down its middle, and the only
; way up is a lookout ledge perched over each bank's outer shoulder. The rock
; targets the two places a round actually happens: the bridge everyone must
; cross, and the right-hand ledge one side climbs to for a look over the
; whole stage. Nothing else on the map is ever hit.
;
; Ground: BankLeft (x=-630..-330) and BankRight (x=330..630), both top y=360.
; They are 660 px apart, too far to fling across directly -- the bridge is
; the crossing, not a shortcut around it.
;
; The bridge: x=-200..200, flush with the banks' own top (y=360), a flat
; 400 px plank. Each side leaves a 130 px gap to the nearest bank edge --
; inside the pickaxe's 150 px reach with a hook to spare, a real fling for
; the sword and dagger, easiest on the staff. RockBridge hangs at the column
; top (0, -430), just above the camera's -450 edge, and drops onto the
; bridge on a timer: crossing is always possible, but camping the middle of
; it is not free. A player who gets caught by the warning steps back onto
; either bank -- the gap is the same 130 px either way -- so the bridge
; never becomes the only route with nowhere to retreat to.
;
; The lookout ledges: HighLedgeLeft (x=-635..-465) and HighLedgeRight
; (x=465..635), both top y=228, sitting almost squarely over each bank's
; outer shoulder -- a 132 px climb, nearly straight up, one hook for the
; pickaxe and a committed effort for the sword or dagger. They are set
; outboard of Spawn0-3 (all inboard, x=-430..430) rather than over them, so
; every spawn opens under open sky, not under a ceiling. RockLedgeRight
; falls on the right one only: the left ledge stays a permanent safe perch
; and vantage point, so a player pressured off the bridge or the right ledge
; always has one piece of high ground nobody is dropping rocks on -- no
; pocket on this stage ever traps a player once the floor starts rising.
;
; Ring-outs: the canyon under the bridge is open sky straight down to the
; kill zone, and the banks are far enough apart that a shove from the bridge
; or from a bank's outer edge sends a player past the far edge and out.
; every_stage_can_ring_out holds the same way Erosion and Gauntlet's canyons
; do -- there is no floor under the gap to catch a bad landing.
;
; All four spawns share one height (y=320, all on the banks), so the rising
; kill zone (ADR-0012) reaches them together -- nobody is left holding lower
; ground than anyone else when the deadline arrives.

; Backdrop (issue #117): quarry.
[node name="Rockfall" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("1")
background_sky_top = Color(0.16, 0.15, 0.16, 1)
background_sky_bottom = Color(0.3, 0.26, 0.22, 1)
background_silhouette = Color(0.16, 0.13, 0.11, 1)
background_layers = PackedStringArray("mountains", "rocks")

; Banks widened outward for issue #137: x=+-330..+-630 -> +-330..+-720.
; The lookout ledges moved out with the banks' outer shoulders (now
; x=+-560..+-720, same height) and RockLedgeRight with its ledge, which
; leaves room for four spawns per bank under open sky. The canyon and
; bridge are untouched.
[node name="BankLeft" parent="." instance=ExtResource("platform")]
position = Vector2(-525, 380)
size = Vector2(390, 40)

[node name="BankRight" parent="." instance=ExtResource("platform")]
position = Vector2(525, 380)
size = Vector2(390, 40)

[node name="Bridge" parent="." instance=ExtResource("platform")]
position = Vector2(0, 372)
size = Vector2(400, 24)

[node name="HighLedgeLeft" parent="." instance=ExtResource("platform")]
position = Vector2(-640, 220)
size = Vector2(160, 24)

[node name="HighLedgeRight" parent="." instance=ExtResource("platform")]
position = Vector2(640, 220)
size = Vector2(160, 24)

; The bridge's rock: column x=0, hanging just above the camera's top edge.
; Defaults (6 s interval, 1.5 s warning, 25 dmg, 28 px radius, 650 px/s
; shove) -- the bridge is the whole stage's crossing, so nothing here needs
; tuning away from the part's own baseline.
[node name="RockBridge" parent="." instance=ExtResource("3")]
position = Vector2(0, -430)

; The right ledge's rock, on a slightly longer interval so its warning
; doesn't always line up with the bridge's -- a player timing one crossing
; still has to watch the other independently. The left ledge gets no rock at
; all: it is this stage's one guaranteed-safe piece of high ground.
[node name="RockLedgeRight" parent="." instance=ExtResource("3")]
position = Vector2(640, -430)
interval_sec = 7.0

